WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.250
Four obligations come before
the first partner goes live.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.723
Privacy: a directory of partner persons,

3
00:00:05.723 --> 00:00:10.818
their access decisions and their sign-in
logs is retrieved by name and identifier,

4
00:00:10.818 --> 00:00:14.415
so whether an existing
system-of-records notice covers it

5
00:00:14.415 --> 00:00:18.012
is the privacy office's
determination, made before go-live.

6
00:00:18.012 --> 00:00:23.278
Minimization: the agency receives only
the attributes its decisions read,

7
00:00:23.278 --> 00:00:26.930
usually a name, a work email,
an immutable identifier,

8
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.412
the partner organization
and, where needed, a role.

9
00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:35.104
Records: NARA's General Records Schedule
3.2 covers system access records,

10
00:00:35.104 --> 00:00:40.411
but the schedules for partner agreements
and access reviews haven't been verified,

11
00:00:40.411 --> 00:00:43.026
so the agency records officer names them.

12
00:00:43.026 --> 00:00:47.970
And redress: a wrong name is corrected
at the partner's source, while an agency

13
00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:52.837
decision, such as a suspension, is
disputed through the agency's own process.

14
00:00:52.837 --> 00:00:58.010
The request and redress workflows
are covered by Section 508, too.
